E'UNILINK PLATFORM\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS OF USE\nVersion 2.0.0 — Effective Date: 19 April 2026\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nPLEASE READ THESE TERMS AND CONDITIONS CAREFULLY BEFORE USING THE UNILINK PLATFORM. BY ACCESSING OR USING THE PLATFORM, YOU CONFIRM THAT YOU HAVE READ, UNDERSTOOD, AND AGREE TO BE LEGALLY BOUND BY THESE TERMS IN THEIR ENTIRETY. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE, YOU MUST IMMEDIATELY CEASE USE OF THE PLATFORM.\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1. DEFINITIONS\n\n1.1 "Platform" means the UniLink mobile and web application, including all software, interfaces, databases, and associated services made available by the Operator.\n\n1.2 "Operator" means the individual developer and owner of UniLink, operating in the Republic of Zimbabwe.\n\n1.3 "Shopper" means any registered individual who uses the Platform to browse goods and submit delivery requests.\n\n1.4 "Delivery Partner" (also "Driver") means any independent contractor registered on the Platform who accepts delivery assignments.\n\n1.5 "Services" means the technology intermediary services provided by the Platform that facilitate communication and coordination between Shoppers and Delivery Partners.\n\n1.6 "Order" means a delivery request submitted by a Shopper through the Platform.\n\n1.7 "Agreement" means these Terms and Conditions together with the Privacy Policy, all policies referenced herein, and any amendments thereto.\n\n\n2. NATURE OF THE PLATFORM — INTERMEDIARY STATUS\n\n2.1 UniLink is strictly a technology intermediary platform. The Operator does NOT:\n  (a) purchase, hold, own, store, or deliver any goods;\n  (b) employ Delivery Partners;\n  (c) guarantee the availability, quality, safety, legality, or fitness for purpose of any goods ordered;\n  (d) guarantee the availability, conduct, competence, or reliability of any Delivery Partner;\n  (e) set or control the prices charged by Delivery Partners for their independent services;\n  (f) act as a principal, agent, employer, franchisor, or partner of any Shopper or Delivery Partner.\n\n2.2 UniLink provides solely a digital matching service enabling Shoppers to identify and communicate with independent Delivery Partners. Any contract for delivery services is formed exclusively between the Shopper and the Delivery Partner. The Operator is not a party to that contract.\n\n2.3 This arrangement is consistent with the definition of an "electronic agent" and "intermediary service provider" under the Electronic Transactions and Electronic Commerce Act [Chapter 12:01] of Zimbabwe.\n\n\n3. ELIGIBILITY AND REGISTRATION\n\n3.1 By registering on the Platform, you represent and warrant that:\n  (a) you are at least 18 years of age;\n  (b) you are legally capable of entering into binding contracts under the laws of Zimbabwe;\n  (c) all information you provide is accurate, current, and complete;\n  (d) you will maintain the accuracy of your information throughout your use of the Platform.\n\n3.2 You are solely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials. Any activity conducted under your account is your sole responsibility.\n\n3.3 The Operator reserves the right to suspend or permanently terminate any account that violates these Terms, without notice and without liability.\n\n\n4. DELIVERY PARTNER TERMS\n\n4.1 Delivery Partners acknowledge and agree that:\n  (a) They are independent contractors and not employees, agents, or representatives of the Operator. Nothing in this Agreement creates an employment relationship, partnership, or joint venture;\n  (b) They are solely responsible for complying with all applicable Zimbabwean laws, including but not limited to the Road Traffic Act [Chapter 13:11], the Labour Act [Chapter 28:01], relevant local authority by-laws, and any licensing requirements;\n  (c) They bear sole responsibility for the safekeeping and delivery of goods once collected;\n  (d) They are responsible for their own taxes, levies, and statutory obligations arising from income earned through the Platform;\n  (e) They must possess valid, current authority to operate any vehicle used for deliveries;\n  (f) They must not misrepresent their identity, location, or availability to Shoppers;\n  (g) The Operator does not guarantee any minimum number of Orders or income.\n\n4.2 Delivery Partners indemnify and hold harmless the Operator from any and all claims, damages, losses, fines, penalties, costs, or expenses (including legal costs) arising from or related to: their acts or omissions; any accident, injury, theft, or damage occurring during a delivery; breach of any law; or any dispute with a Shopper.\n\n\n5. SHOPPER TERMS\n\n5.1 Shoppers acknowledge and agree that:\n  (a) The Operator does not guarantee that any specific Delivery Partner will accept their Order;\n  (b) Estimated delivery times are indicative only and are not binding commitments;\n  (c) The Operator bears no responsibility for the quality, correctness, completeness, freshness, or safety of goods purchased from any third-party shop or vendor;\n  (d) Shoppers are responsible for providing accurate delivery addresses and contact information;\n  (e) Payment disputes between Shoppers and Delivery Partners must be resolved directly between those parties;\n  (f) The Operator is not responsible for any loss arising from a Shopper providing incorrect item descriptions, quantities, or delivery instructions.\n\n5.2 Shoppers indemnify and hold harmless the Operator from any and all claims, damages, losses, costs, or expenses arising from: their acts or omissions; inaccurate or incomplete Order information; disputes with Delivery Partners; or any third-party claims related to goods ordered.\n\n\n6. PAYMENTS\n\n6.1 All financial transactions for delivery services (including delivery fees and payments for goods) are conducted directly between the Shopper and the Delivery Partner.\n\n6.2 The Operator does not collect, hold, process, or transfer payment funds on behalf of any party and accepts no liability for payment disputes, failed transactions, or fraud between Shoppers and Delivery Partners.\n\n6.3 The Operator may, at its discretion, display indicative fee ranges for informational purposes only; these do not constitute a binding quotation.\n\n\n7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n\n7.1 TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, INCLUDING THE CONSUMER PROTECTION ACT [CHAPTER 14:44] OF ZIMBABWE, THE OPERATOR, ITS DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, CONTRACTORS, AND AGENTS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR:\n  (a) ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, PUNITIVE, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES;\n  (b) LOSS OF GOODS, MONEY, GOODWILL, OR DATA;\n  (c) PERSONAL INJURY OR DEATH (EXCEPT WHERE CAUSED BY THE OPERATOR\'S GROSS NEGLIGENCE OR WILFUL MISCONDUCT);\n  (d) DELAYS, FAILURES, ERRORS, OR INTERRUPTIONS IN THE PLATFORM;\n  (e) THE CONDUCT, ACTS, OR OMISSIONS OF ANY SHOPPER OR DELIVERY PARTNER;\n  (f) ANY GOODS PURCHASED THROUGH THE PLATFORM.\n\n7.2 Where liability cannot be excluded by law, the Operator\'s aggregate liability to any user for all claims arising in any 12-month period shall not exceed the total platform fees (if any) paid by that user to the Operator during that period, or USD 10.00, whichever is greater.\n\n7.3 The Platform is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis without any warranty of any kind, whether express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.\n\n\n8. FORCE MAJEURE\n\n8.1 The Operator shall not be liable for any failure or delay in performance caused by circumstances beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, government actions, power outages, internet disruptions, civil unrest, or pandemics.\n\n\n9. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n\n9.1 All intellectual property in the Platform — including software, design, trademarks, logos, and content — belongs exclusively to the Operator. Users are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the Platform solely for its intended purpose.\n\n9.2 Users may not reverse-engineer, copy, reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works from any part of the Platform without the Operator\'s prior written consent.\n\n\n10. PROHIBITED CONDUCT\n\n10.1 Users must not:\n  (a) Use the Platform for any unlawful purpose;\n  (b) Submit false, misleading, or fraudulent information;\n  (c) Harass, threaten, or abuse any other user;\n  (d) Attempt to circumvent security features;\n  (e) Introduce malware, viruses, or harmful code;\n  (f) Use the Platform to arrange the delivery of prohibited, illegal, or controlled goods.\n\n10.2 Violations may result in immediate account termination and may be reported to law enforcement authorities.\n\n\n11. DISPUTE RESOLUTION\n\n11.1 Disputes between a Shopper and a Delivery Partner are solely between those parties. The Operator has no obligation to mediate, arbitrate, or resolve such disputes.\n\n11.2 Any dispute between a User and the Operator shall first be submitted to good-faith negotiation. If unresolved within 30 days, the dispute shall be referred to arbitration in Harare, Zimbabwe, under the Arbitration Act [Chapter 7:15], with proceedings conducted in English. The arbitral award shall be final and binding.\n\n11.3 Nothing in this clause prevents the Operator from seeking urgent injunctive relief in any competent court.\n\n\n12. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION\n\n12.1 This Agreement is governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Zimbabwe.\n\n12.2 Subject to clause 11, the parties irrevocably submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Zimbabwe.\n\n\n13. AMENDMENTS\n\n13.1 The Operator may amend these Terms at any time. Users will be notified through the Platform and must re-accept updated Terms to continue using the Platform. Continued use after re-acceptance constitutes agreement to the revised Terms.\n\n\n14. SEVERABILITY\n\n14.1 If any provision of this Agreement is found to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.\n\n\n15. ENTIRE AGREEMENT\n\n15.1 This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the User and the Operator with respect to the Platform and supersedes all prior agreements, representations, or understandings.\n\n\n16. CONTACT\n\n16.1 For queries, complaints, or notices, contact the Operator through the in-app Support section.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nBy tapping "Accept & Continue", you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions and the Privacy Policy.\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━',

