E'UNILINK PLATFORM\nPRIVACY POLICY\nVersion 2.0.0 — Effective Date: 19 April 2026\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n1. INTRODUCTION\n\n1.1 UniLink ("we", "us", "our") is committed to protecting the privacy of all users in accordance with the Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07] of Zimbabwe ("the Act") and the Postal and Telecommunications Act [Chapter 12:05].\n\n1.2 This Privacy Policy explains what personal data we collect, how we use it, and your rights in respect of that data.\n\n\n2. DATA WE COLLECT\n\n2.1 Registration Data: Full name, phone number, university/campus location, and account credentials.\n\n2.2 Transaction Data: Order details, delivery addresses, preferred payment methods, and order history.\n\n2.3 Location Data: GPS coordinates (where permission is granted) used solely to facilitate delivery matching.\n\n2.4 Device & Usage Data: Device type, IP address, browser/app version, and interaction logs, collected for platform security and improvement.\n\n2.5 Communications: Messages sent through the in-app chat feature.\n\n2.6 Acceptance Records: Records of when you accepted these Terms and the applicable version.\n\n\n3. HOW WE USE YOUR DATA\n\n3.1 We use your personal data to:\n  (a) Create and manage your account;\n  (b) Match Shoppers with available Delivery Partners;\n  (c) Process and display order information;\n  (d) Send transactional notifications;\n  (e) Ensure platform security and prevent fraud;\n  (f) Comply with legal obligations;\n  (g) Improve platform performance and user experience.\n\n3.2 We do not sell, rent, or lease your personal data to third parties for marketing purposes.\n\n\n4. LEGAL BASIS FOR PROCESSING\n\n4.1 We process your data on the following legal bases:\n  (a) Contractual necessity — to perform the Services you have requested;\n  (b) Compliance with a legal obligation — where processing is required by Zimbabwean law;\n  (c) Legitimate interests — to protect the platform, prevent fraud, and improve our services, provided these interests are not overridden by your rights.\n\n\n5. DATA SHARING\n\n5.1 We share data only as necessary:\n  (a) With Delivery Partners — Shoppers\' names, phone numbers, and delivery location are shared with the matched Delivery Partner solely to fulfil an Order;\n  (b) With Shoppers — Delivery Partners\' names, phone numbers, and profile pictures are shared with the Shopper for the purpose of the delivery;\n  (c) With service providers — we use Supabase (a cloud database platform) to store data securely. Supabase processes data subject to its own security and privacy standards;\n  (d) With authorities — where required by law, court order, or lawful government request.\n\n5.2 We do not share your data for any other purpose without your explicit consent.\n\n\n6. DATA RETENTION\n\n6.1 We retain personal data for as long as your account remains active and for a period of 5 years thereafter, or as required by applicable Zimbabwean law.\n\n6.2 Order data and chat records are retained for a minimum of 2 years for dispute resolution purposes.\n\n6.3 You may request deletion of your account and associated data by contacting us through the Support section. We will process requests within 30 days subject to any legal retention obligations.\n\n\n7. DATA SECURITY\n\n7.1 We implement industry-standard technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data, including encrypted data transmission, row-level database security, and access controls.\n\n7.2 No method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure. While we strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your data, we cannot guarantee absolute security.\n\n7.3 In the event of a data breach that poses a risk to your rights and freedoms, we will notify affected users and the relevant Zimbabwean authority as required under the Cyber and Data Protection Act.\n\n\n8. YOUR RIGHTS\n\n8.1 Under the Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07], you have the right to:\n  (a) Access the personal data we hold about you;\n  (b) Correct inaccurate or incomplete data;\n  (c) Request deletion of your data, subject to legal retention requirements;\n  (d) Object to processing on grounds of legitimate interests;\n  (e) Lodge a complaint with the Postal and Telecommunications Regulatory Authority of Zimbabwe (POTRAZ).\n\n8.2 To exercise these rights, contact us through the in-app Support section. We will respond within 30 days.\n\n\n9. PUSH NOTIFICATIONS\n\n9.1 We may send push notifications relating to your Orders and platform updates. You may withdraw consent for notifications at any time through your device settings or the app notification settings.\n\n\n10. CHILDREN\n\n10.1 The Platform is not intended for use by persons under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors. If we become aware that a minor has registered, we will delete their data promptly.\n\n\n11. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY\n\n11.1 We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be communicated through the Platform and will require re-acceptance before continued use.\n\n\n12. CONTACT\n\n12.1 For privacy-related queries, contact us through the in-app Support section.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThis Privacy Policy is read together with and forms part of the UniLink Terms and Conditions.\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━',

